00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.330
Banana Sundae                         Pudding A la Moce         Double White Sandwich

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.330
But...

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.200
Oh. That department store, huh?

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.040
That's right! We should go, too!

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:55.950
Yeah. I guess we should before it closes.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.620
"Closes"? It's going belly-up?!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.160
Well, it's an old building

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.160
and there aren't many customers, right?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.790
What are you talking about? It's great

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.790
BECAUSE it's old and there aren't many customers!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.580
That's no way for the stores to stay open, is it?

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.200
Nice! I got "Excellent Luck"!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.790
As did I!

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.200
My brother is a liar...

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:27.580
There's not a single sign that says they're closing.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:32.580
Sure, there aren't many customers,

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:32.580
but it's still got some life left in it.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.540
Places like this make you hope

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.540
they stick around, don't they?

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:47.370
So that even once you and I have become adults,

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:47.370
we can reminisce and talk about "that time when."

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:53.200
And as we're talking, we can think to ourselves,

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:53.200
"I'm glad we became friends."

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:55.830
TSF...

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:01.040
D-don't you worry. This is staying put.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:01.040
Nothing's going to change!

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:17.580
Huh?

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.700
What is it, Ebina?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.950
Was that always a vacant lot?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.660
Oh, you're right. That's a lot of empty land...

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.790
I wonder if some big building used to be there.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.410
There used to be... an amusement park there.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.700
Huh? An amusement park?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.450
Yes. It was most fun, indeed!

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.450
That's when I first realized...

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.200
Where should we go?

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.330
Well then, UMR! There is somewhere that I wish to go!

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:04.790
Sylphin knew that the department store

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:04.790
would be closing.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:11.120
Hey, how about we all go to the amusement park

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:11.120
on our next day off?

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.790
I would like to go, indeed!

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.500
I-I will go, too!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.410
Where should we go?

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.870
This familiar scenery....

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:25.750
Once we become adults, it will have changed completely.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:31.450
But even if the scenery changes,

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:31.450
there are some things that will never change...

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:36.250
Because they exist in our memories.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.290
Coming!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.830
Ah, Ebina. Good morning.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:52.450
U-um! I got some rice in the mail, from Akita.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:53.870
This year as well?

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.040
Thanks, as always.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:01.370
Thanks, Ebina. You should join us for dinner tonight!

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.540
O-okay! Thank you!

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.330
I have to make sure I don't eat too much...

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.750
What should I make today...?

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:14.830
This is new crop rice, right?

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:14.830
I should make something extra tasty...

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.080
What do YOU always make, Ebina?

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:24.040
Um, if I'm using rice, kiritanpo hotpot, or...

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:24.040
oh, oyaki dumplings.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.080
Oh. Yeah, you're from Akita all right.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:33.370
Still, you need mochi rice for oyaki,

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:33.370
and kiritanpo takes a lot of time to make.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.790
If we're going to make something in time for lunch...

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:38.160
Ah!

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:40.580
What about takikomi rice?

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:42.160
Whoa! Good idea!

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.540
AKITA

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.540
AKITA KOMACHI RICE

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.700
Sorry to drag you into the kitchen,

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.700
but you'll be a big help.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.950
I-I'm in the kitchen with Taihei!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.870
Are you okay, Ebina?

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.200
Th-th-this is...

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.410
It's like what Kirie said before!

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:01.040
Ebina! I have a cunning plan!

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.040
Huh? A "plan"?

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.200
Apparently, the way to a man's heart

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.200
is through his stomach.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.120
His stomach?!

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.790
Put simply, through FOOD!

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:12.620
Feed Taihei some of your home cooking

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:12.620
and you'll land him for sure!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.330
L-l-land him?! No, I can't!

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:18.620
Land him!

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.830
Land him! Land him! For sure!

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:19.540
Land him!

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:19.540
Land him!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:20.830
Land him!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:20.830
Land him!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:20.830
For \sure!!

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.040
She's really concentrating hard.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.160
Is that from being from a farming family?

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.120
Ebina, I'll help too.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.160
Okay!

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.000
Don't you think it's a little cramped?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.540
No, it's fine!

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:40.450
If I let her cook alone with Big Brother,

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:40.450
she'll find out HE'S the one who always makes the food.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.870
I have to help out, at least a little.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:48.700
Ebina, I'll trim the chicken and dice the vegetables.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:48.700
Would you mind rinsing the rice?

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.580
Oh, um, okay!

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.830
What about me?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.620
Well, we're going to cook the chicken,

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.620
so you can get the frypan ready.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.540
Leave it to me, Big Brother!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.250
She should be able to do that, at least...

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.250
He's so close!

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.200
Brother, how about this?

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:14.160
No, that's too small. It's for frying eggs.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:19.200
I-I knew that! I was just joking.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.450
The larger one's down below there,

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.450
so go ahead and add some oil for me.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.910
Ah... Must be nice...

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.120
Land him!

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:32.040
Kirie... Sure enough, I can't do it!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.250
Fire!

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.330
Ebina!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.750
Are you okay, Ebina?

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.250
Dammit, Umaru!

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:53.410
You gave Ebina such a shock that she fell!

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:53.410
What if she'd hurt herself?!

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:57.250
And why did you add that much oil

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:57.250
just for browning the chicken?

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:00.290
Uh, I got a little confused...

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:04.000
I-I'm sorry, Ebina. Are you okay?

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.870
The truth is, I can't cook at all.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.910
I wanted to grab him... but he grabbed me!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:11.620
Huh?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.410
Well, that little accident aside...

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:23.160
Y-yes! I'm sorry!

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:25.000
No, it was my fault.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.450
Okay then...

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.500
Let's eat!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:41.700
MoguMogu the

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:41.700
Severed Head

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:41.700
Potato Chips

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.370
I wonder what's for dinner tonight...

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:38.120
Thursday is bread day, so what could it be?

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.080
I'm home.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.700
Oh, Big Brother!

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:47.330
Look who I ran into on the way home.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:47.330
So, I invited her over for dinner.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.200
"Ran into," you say? And where

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.200
did this meeting take place?

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.410
What are you all mad about?

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.410
Was it wrong for me to come, Big Brother?

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.830
No, you're perfectly fine.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.120
Ah! That was a sneer!

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.620
It was her PLAN to come here, Big Brother!

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.790
It was just a coincidence, Big Brother.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.160
What difference does it make?

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.250
And what's got you so angry?

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.120
You're acting strange.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.370
She's had dinner with us before, right?

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:27.200
Yeah, but still...

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.080
Well? Why did you come here?

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.290
It was just a coincidence.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.330
I saw him as he was leaving the office,

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.620
so I called out "Big Brother!" and he replied "Hikari!"

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.330
BIG BROTHER!

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:44.700
HIKARI

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:44.700
BIG BROTHER!

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.660
THAT'S NOT A COINCIDENCE AT ALL!

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:49.700
I just happened to be outside of his office

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:49.700
and he just happened to come out.

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.200
There's nothing coincidental about that!

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.450
It's purely coincidental.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:56.160
I thought those two were friends...

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:00.450
What's got Umaru in such a bad mood?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:06.700
Still, maybe Hikari came over so they can get closer.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.410
HOKKAIDO

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.410
MILK

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.410
HOKKAIDO

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.410
MILK

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:15.580
Huh? Isn't it bread day today?

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:19.450
Yup, it's bread day. So, let's make pancakes.

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:23.950
Okay, I think it's ready now.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.830
All of us making something together

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.830
will probably help them break the ice.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.160
Okay, who's up first?

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.370
I... I-!

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:36.870
Okay! I shall make you the perfect pancake, Big Brother!

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.450
"Perfect," huh? That's a tall order.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.000
Nah, it's easy!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.200
All you have to do is pour this on here!

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:44.450
You think?

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:48.910
Hyaa!

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.080
It was too soon!

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.290
GLOP~

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.290
Opening Move: Umaru

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:58.410
Big Brother, I can make a better one.

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.580
Um, Hikari?

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.700
BURNT~

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.700
Follow-up: Hikari

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:19.500
You watching?

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:22.580
The trick is to wait until the surface starts to bubble.

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:25.700
TOPPED WITH ICE CREAM!

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:25.700
Okay, all done!

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:27.790
What is this sorcery?!

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:34.750
Delish!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.540
It's fun to make food together, isn't it?

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:41.370
Huh? Did you make more?

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:46.620
No, these are your two.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:46.620
You said you made them for me, right?

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:53.450
Big Brother, don't force yourself.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:53.450
There's no way those will taste good.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.200
Um, I...

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:56.870
Hm?

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:01.290
I came because I wanted to eat bread with you.

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:01.290
It wasn't a coincidence.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.330
I'm sorry for lying.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:06.580
You don't say...

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.120
Oh, that's right!

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:20.750
You forgot this last time!

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.950
That's pretty incredible that you got an award.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.160
Th-thank you very much.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.120
Hmph!

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.790
I GOT AN AWARD TOO!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.370
Why are you getting so mad?

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:33.120
I'm not getting mad!

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.950
Mine is for AP classes.

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:38.330
They recommended that I take AP classes too!

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:39.660
See? You're getting mad.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.950
I'M NOT GETTING MAD!

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:51.790
Squeak, squeak. Hamjiro, Hamsaburo, c'mon!

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.080
Ding-ding-ding!

00:18:55.330 --> 00:19:00.750
Ooh, and the wild hamsters have appeared!

00:18:55.330 --> 00:19:00.750
Let's get your hamster ball ready!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.750
Dammit, Umaru! Don't treat your hamsters like toys!

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:09.250
Y-you've got it all wrong, Big Brother.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:09.250
We're just playing together.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.870
Even if you're trying to play,

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.870
your pets aren't having any fun.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:15.450
I mean, look at their faces.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.910
They're making the same face as always...

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:24.660
Look, small animals have been known to die from stress.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:31.370
They're always in the same place, inside their cage.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:31.370
You have to treat them with care, right?

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:33.160
Y-yeah...

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.250
The next day

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.870
Master! Good afternoon!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.500
And good afternoon, hamsters.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:43.580
Master, are you not letting them out today?

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.330
Yeah. 'Cause Big Brother said...

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.620
Pet stress?

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:53.410
Yeah, he thinks I tire them out

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:53.410
by playing with them too much.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:59.620
A-a long time ago at an aquarium I went to,

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:59.620
I heard that even fish can feel stress.

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.500
All those people coming and going

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.500
and standing there in front of them...

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:07.500
Well, the hamsters always stay inside the house,

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:07.500
so I think they're okay!

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.790
The following day

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:13.160
Hamjiro, Hamsaburo, good afternoon.

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:15.290
The following following day

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:17.120
'Sup, Tanukichi?

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.290
The following following following day

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:21.790
I'll be back.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.450
Okay, here's your food.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.250
Sorry Hamjiro and Hamsaburo...

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.830
Umaru must be tough to put up with.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.700
She's a bit selfish, but don't hold it against her, okay?

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:42.080
Huh? What's wrong?

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:50.700
Umaru has returned!

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:55.450
Okay, I'm back! Games, Internet, and anime!

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:04.200
Hamjiro, Hamsaburo, c'mon out! Let's have a party!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.620
Well, that was the usual fun and games...

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:18.910
What should we do next?

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:18.910
Still, it's not like you can understand me.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.660
You're not feeling any stress, right?

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:28.830
I wonder if Big Brother will be home soon...

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:34.330
Huh? Your hamster ball?

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:38.500
Well, well! You two wanna play with me after all!

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:43.080
Okay! Today it's the Pokéham the Movie 2000!

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:45.870
I'm home.

